e'], df['sales'])\", status_message=\"Creating sales timeline plot\")\n\nComplex Request: \"Build comprehensive sales analysis with predictions\"\n→ CreatePlan([Data loading, EDA, trend analysis, forecasting model, visualization])\n\nClarification Needed: \"Analyze the data\" (no specifics)\n→ RespondToUser(message=\"I'd be happy to analyze your data. Could you specify what type of analysis you're looking for?\", intent=\"clarification\")\n\nPlan Execution: User edited cards and said \"proceed\"\n→ Execute first edited card step with insert_and_execute_cell\n\nTask Complete: Analysis finished with results\n→ RespondToUser(message=\"Analysis complete. Results show...\", intent=\"completion\")\n\nThe conversation history shows you everything - read it naturally and respond appropriately to the user's current intent.", "role": "system"}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Current Context:\n--------\nNotebook Context Guide:\n\nThe notebook state below shows ALL cells with their ACTUAL indices (0-based). This includes:\n- Code cells (executed and not executed)\n- Markdown cells\n- Empty cells\n- Images from plots/charts (you can see these images directly)\n\nCRITICAL INDEX USAGE:\n- Cell indices shown as \"Cell [N]\" are 0-based positions in the notebook\n- When using delete_cell(cell_index), use the EXACT index N shown in \"Cell [N]\"\n- Do NOT skip or renumber - use the index exactly as shown\n\nCell Status Indicators:\n- ✅ Code cell (executed #N) = Cell was run successfully (execution count N)\n- ✅ Code cell (executed #N) with outputs = Cell produced results/plots/data\n- ⏸️ Code cell (not executed) = Code cell exists but hasn't been run yet\n- 📝 Markdown cell = Documentation/text cell\n- Empty cells are shown with no content after the cell header\n\nCurrent Notebook State:\nAll Notebook Cells (0-based indexing):\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Cell [0]: ⏸️ Code cell (not executed)\n\n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Cell [1]: ✅ Code cell (executed #1)\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Cell [2]: ✅ Code cell (executed #2) with outputs\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Generate synthetic data\ndef generate_dummy_data(num_samples=1000):\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    \n    # Generate random data\n    data = {\n        'customer_id': range(1, num_samples + 1),\n        'age': np.random.randint(18, 70, size=num_samples),\n        'gender': np.random.choice(['Male', 'Female'], size=num_samples),\n        'tenure': np.random.randint(1, 72, size=num_samples),\n        'balance': np.random.uniform(0, 10000, size=num_samples),\n        'products_number': np.random.randint(1, 5, size=num_samples),\n        'credit_score': np.random.randint(300, 850, size=num_samples),\n        'active_member': np.random.choice([0, 1], size=num_samples),\n        'estimated_salary': np.random.uniform(20000, 120000, size=num_samples),\n        'churn': np.random.choice([0, 1], size=num_samples, p=[0.8, 0.2])\n    }\n    \n    return pd.DataFrame(data)\n\n# Create the dataset\ndummy_data = generate_dummy_data()\ndummy_data.head()\n  Outputs:\n    📊 Result:    customer_id  age  gender  tenure      balance  products_number  \\\n0            1   56    Male      40  8278.683753                3   \n1            2   69    Male      45  7877.130155                2   \n2            3   46    Male      62  6244.254465                2   \n3            4   32  Female      58  4944.811313                3   \n4            5   60    Male      67  9795.508404                3   \n\n   credit_score  active_member  estimated_salary  churn  \n0           784              1      86170.384548      0  \n1           383              1      41912.606467      0  \n2           595              1      31284.318718      1  \n3           535              0      79643.395463      0  \n4           355              1      68468.951694      0  \n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Cell [3]: ✅ Code cell (executed #3) with outputs\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\n# Display basic statistics\nprint(dummy_data.describe())\n\n# Plot distribution of numerical features\nplt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\ndummy_data.hist(bins=30, figsize=(14, 8), layout=(2, 5))\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# Plot correlation heatmap\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\nsns.heatmap(dummy_data.corr(), annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='coolwarm')\nplt.title('Correlation Heatmap')\nplt.show()\n  Outputs:\n    📝 stdout:        customer_id         age       tenure      balance  products_number  \\\ncount  1000.000000  1000.00000  1000.000000  1000.000000      1000.000000   \nmean    500.500000    43.81900    34.627000  5063.485175         2.485000   \nstd     288.819436    14.99103    20.334782  2910.640148         1.099538   \nmin       1.000000    18.00000     1.000000     1.883996         1.000000   \n25%     250.750000    31.00000    17.000000  2535.692101         2.000000   \n50%     500.500000    44.00000    33.500000  5188.934123         2.000000   \n75%     750.250000    56.00000    52.000000  7599.221577         3.000000   \nmax    1000.000000    69.00000    71.000000  9997.138042         4.000000   \n\n       credit_score  active_member  estimated_salary        churn  \ncount   1000.000000    1000.000000       1000.000000  1000.000000  \nmean     577.482000       0.488000      68635.960668     0.188000  \nstd      156.282648       0.500106      29174.136963     0.390908  \nmin      300.000000       0.000000      20074.770837     0.000000  \n25%      445.000000       0.000000      43589.451149     0.000000  \n50%      577.000000       0.000000      67589.297919     0.000000  \n75%      720.000000       1.000000      93916.479816     0.000000  \nmax      849.000000       1.000000     119904.949810     1.000000  \n\n    📊 Result: <Figure size 1400x800 with 0 Axes>\n    📊 Result: <Figure size 1400x800 with 10 Axes>\n"}, {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "data:image/png;base64,"}}, {"type": "t