Cell [6]: ✅ Code cell (executed #6) with outputs\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix\n\n# Making predictions\ny_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n\n# Evaluating the model\naccuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\nconf_matrix = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\nclass_report = classification_report(y_test, y_pred)\n\naccuracy, conf_matrix, class_report\n  Outputs:\n    📊 Result: (0.84,\n array([[166,   1],\n        [ 31,   2]]),\n '              precision    recall  f1-score   support\\n\\n           0       0.84      0.99      0.91       167\\n           1       0.67      0.06      0.11        33\\n\\n    accuracy                           0.84       200\\n   macro avg       0.75      0.53      0.51       200\\nweighted avg       0.81      0.84      0.78       200\\n')\n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "\nCRITICAL: Use the notebook state to understand what work has already been completed. You can SEE the actual plots and charts that were generated. Current Iteration: 8"}], "role": "user"}, {"content": "can you conduct a customer churn analysis based on dummy data for me", "role": "user"}, {"content": "Final plan that needs to be implemented:\n\n[CARD:Generate Dummy Data|Create a synthetic dataset with customer information and churn status.]\n[CARD:Data Exploration|Perform exploratory data analysis (EDA) to understand the dataset.]\n[CARD:Feature Engineering|Prepare the data for modeling by creating relevant features.]\n[CARD:Model Building|Train a machine learning model to predict customer churn.]\n[CARD:Model Evaluation|Evaluate the model's performance using appropriate metrics.]\n[CARD:Visualization|Visualize the results and key insights.]", "role": "user"}, {"content": "Also add code to suppress all the warnings in scikit-learn before you implement all these models otherwise the plan logs could proceed.", "role": "user"}, {"content": "Final plan that needs to be implemented:\n\n[CARD:Generate Dummy Data|Create a synthet